Subject: wifi: mt76: recognize host NAN in the pinned MT7925 20261016 WM

The public image lacks bit 5 but produces real DW_START/DW_END and iPad
service discovery with the host NAN ABI. Match its path, size, feature byte
and build date. Firmware installation independently checks its pinned SHA-256.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt792x_core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt792x_core.c
@@ -934,6 +934,17 @@
 		data += le16_to_cpu(rel_info->len) + rel_info->pad_len;
 	}
 
+	/* This pinned public WM implements host NAN (including DW events), but
+	 * its release-info feature byte omits NAN. Limit the correction to the
+	 * verified MT7925 image; other firmware keeps its advertised features.
+	 */
+	if (!strcmp(fw_wm, MT7925_FIRMWARE_WM) &&
+	    fw->size == 1390712 && offload_caps == MT792x_FW_CAP_CNM &&
+	    !memcmp(hdr->build_date, "20261016233029", 14)) {
+		offload_caps |= MT792x_FW_CAP_NAN;
+		dev_info(dev, "NAN capability correction for WM 20261016233029\n");
+	}
+
 out:
 	release_firmware(fw);
 
